PREAMBLE = "CLOUD CONCEPT INVENTORY (draft form, Round 4)\nEach question has exactly one best answer. Terms are vendor-neutral:\n- Virtual network: an isolated private network in a cloud account (e.g. VPC, VNet). A subnet is an address range in it; each subnet uses one route table.\n- Internet gateway: the virtual network's attachment to the public internet. NAT gateway: a managed network-address-translation service.\n- Host firewall: allow-rules attached to one virtual machine or its network interface. It tracks connections (stateful).\n- Subnet ACL: numbered allow/deny rules attached to a subnet. It does not track connections (stateless).\n- Identity policy: permissions attached to a user or role. Resource policy: permissions attached to a resource (e.g. a bucket), naming which principals may act on it.\n- Organisation guardrail: a policy set by an organisation for a whole account. Permission boundary: a policy attached to a role that sets its maximum permissions.\n- Bucket: a container in an object-storage service; objects are files stored in a bucket.\n- Authorisation on this platform: when the caller and the resource are in the same account, a grant in either the caller's identity policy or the resource's policy is enough; when they are in different accounts, both are needed (an identity-policy grant in the caller's account and a resource-policy grant on the resource).\n- Private DNS zone: a DNS zone holding private names, which can be linked to virtual networks (e.g. a private hosted zone, a private DNS zone, or a private Cloud DNS zone).\n"
